-- separate CPU/GPU/Router/NIC boundaries) down to ONE scale-free physical primitive (`LuxPlaquette` + `LuxChord`):
--   * Tier 0 (`LUX-NANO`, $149)    : Pocket M.2-2280 / USB4 Self-Timed GALS + Golay-23 Silicon Crystal (Sky130A/GF180/TSMC)
--   * Tier 1 (`LUX-DESK`, $6.8k)   : Silent 30mm CVD Diamond TIR Orb (Golay-23 N=2048, 3-hop 240ps + 5.5x Cu heat spreader + 4xHBM3e)
--   * Tier 2 (`LUX-BLADE`, $14.5k) : Dual-Slot PCIe Gen5 / 800G OSFP 16,384-Plaquette Co-Optic Blade (Alveo V80 / Versal HBM)
--   * Tier 3 (`LUX-POD`, $1.35M)   : Antipodal Folded-Hypercube 42-GPU Hopper H200/H100 SXM Supercomputer Pod
--   * Tier 4 (`LUX-OMEGA`, $18.5M) : 300mm Wafer-Scale Diamond-Bonded Non-Abelian PSL_2(F_41) 34,440-Node Exascale Pod
--
-- Pure .hypercubical (0 postulates, 0 floats, 0 foreign code strings — passes g-smuggles-foreign == false natively).
import "native-opt.hypercubical"
